    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Schrödinger's cat was designed to expose a problem, not propose a blurry animal. The missing actor is the environment, which destroys observable interference almost instantly.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Why don't we observe a cat in a live-dead superposition?",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — DECOHERENCE",
            "segment": "The Cat and Its Environment",
            "greeting": "Shalom, Liam",
            "runningText": "tracking which-branch information…",
            "output": [
              "Environment records distinguishable branch information.",
              "Interference becomes locally inaccessible."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "In the ideal thought experiment, one microscopic event becomes correlated with two macroscopic records: live cat and dead cat. Quantum theory treats the combined system as a superposition.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "To reveal that superposition, the live and dead branches would need to remain coherent and later recombine. Only then could their amplitudes produce interference.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "A real cat cannot be isolated. Air molecules, thermal photons, the box, and internal degrees of freedom continually interact with it.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Those interactions correlate different environmental states with the two branches. In effect, the surroundings acquire which-branch information without a person opening the box.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "As those environmental records become distinguishable, the branch overlap collapses toward zero. The interference that would connect live and dead becomes inaccessible to local experiments.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "This is decoherence. For ordinary macroscopic objects in ordinary environments, it is fantastically fast, but the exact time depends on size, separation, temperature, and coupling.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The system then behaves, for practical local predictions, like a classical mixture of alternatives. That does not mean the full system-plus-environment state literally chose one branch.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Decoherence also helps explain the preferred basis. The interaction selects stable pointer states — here, macroscopically distinct records — rather than arbitrary live-plus-dead combinations.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "But it does not solve the outcome problem. Suppressing interference explains why branches do not look blurred together; it does not, by itself, explain why one particular outcome is experienced.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Does decoherence select the observed result, or select the stable basis in which alternatives stop interfering? Pause before the answer: it explains the stable basis and lost interference, not the unique outcome.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: state what decoherence does and does not explain.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Basis Versus Outcome",
            "greeting": "Your move, Liam",
            "runningText": "separating two measurement problems…",
            "output": [
              "Explains: stable pointer basis and lost local interference.",
              "Does not select: the unique observed outcome."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:51:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Why the cat isn't both alive and dead: the environment makes the branches unable to interfere, long before anyone looks.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "fade"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
